## M0 Scope and precedence

Reuse complete-manual package proposal revision2, PACCMP02/version2/suite1. It is offline interchange, not PACC wire, root codec, authority, registry or store. This candidate only freezes the concrete envelope/ZIP/metadata rules below if subsequently accepted. Existing manual custody exception and automatic client-local custody remain accepted and unchanged. Internal CA profile1 is the normal issuer; earlier proposal language suggesting an arbitrarily selected external CA does not override that decision. Active-Session revocation remains POLICY_PENDING; no Stop-on-revoke rule is accepted here.

Package format availability grants no key generation, signature, issuance, export, operational CURRENT, recovery or admission. Missing crypto backend, factual administrative authorization, same-root CURRENT, issuer/signing delegation, serial reservation, recipient approval or budget denies generation. Offline data parsing is not RESOLVED or trust approval. No production migration or prior PCP1 fallback is permitted.

## M1 Concrete existing suite, subject to explicit acceptance

Use the EXISTING PROPOSED suite, not a new construction: ChaCha20-Poly1305 RFC8439 key32/nonce12/tag16; PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 dkLen32, salt16, exactly600000 iterations; RSA2048/e65537 RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 SHA256 package signature256. No algorithm/iteration/tag/key-size downgrade or alternative suite search. Standard vetted implementation artifacts must be selected/licensed/pinned and qualified, never a handwritten crypto primitive or invented BearSSL/PST API. API/source availability is not VC6/NT4 qualification. Failed backend/cancellation/credit qualification denies effects; it does not tune parameters.

Unlock secret is20 CSPRNG bytes encoded as exactly32 RFC4648 uppercase Base32 A-Z2-7, no padding. This suite does not accept user-chosen weak passwords. For input only, strip ASCII spaces and hyphens, fold ASCII lowercase, then require exactly32 valid characters; PBKDF2 input is those32 ASCII bytes. No other whitespace, Unicode/locale normalization or CLI/environment secret transport. Use fresh approved random password/salt/nonce for each new protected package. Re-export copies exact protected bytes; reprotection requires a new authorized transaction and fresh randomness. Package and unlock secret use distinct approved delivery. Three failed unlocks per UI session require explicit close/reopen; this is not offline brute-force prevention or global single-use.

Authenticate independent approved signer before KDF; verify AEAD tag before parsing/using plaintext. Internal in-place AEAD output stays quarantined until tag success and is wiped after failure/quiescence. Full tag comparison and wipe use reviewed non-elidable/constant-time facilities. Signature uses a dedicated administratively delegated package key distinct from CA, channel and client keys; accepted codeSigning certificate purpose must be established by the approved signer context. File-supplied SPKI/hash, password or included CA does not authenticate that context. First Browser may enter independently authenticated full signer fingerprint/server confirmation without a second material file or prior CSR; absent verified purpose/delegation/fingerprint reference denies import.

## M2 Exact outer envelope

Integers are unsigned big endian; no native struct serialization. Header92 bytes: offsets0:8 ASCII PACCMP02;8:u16 version2;10:u16 suite1;12:u32 flags0;16:u32 total;20:u32 ciphertext_length;24:u32 iterations600000;28:16 salt;44:12 nonce;56:32 SHA256 of exact complete signer DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo;88:u32 SPKI_length. SPKI starts92, length1..1024, strict RSA2048/e65537 DER, one complete value and no trailing bytes.

Let S=SPKI_length, C=ciphertext_length. Ciphertext at92+S, length1..65536. Tag16 at92+S+C. Signature256 at108+S+C. Exact total=364+S+C, <=131072; no padding, trailer or ambiguous version detection. Bounds/checked arithmetic precede allocation or expensive crypto. Unknown flags/version/suite, noncanonical/unsupported SPKI, truncation or trailing bytes reject the entire package.

AAD is exact bytes[0,92+S). Signed bytes are the exact25 ASCII bytes PAPACC-COMPLETE-MANUAL-V2, one ZERO byte, followed by exact file bytes[0,108+S+C), including tag. Signature is excluded from its own input. File SHA256 is transfer/audit correlation only. Hold immutable input/native object identity across verification and use; never reread a replaceable path as the verified package.

## M3 Exact protected archive and metadata

Plaintext is exactly one ZIP32 STORE archive, five entries in order: ca.der, cliente.der, cliente.pk8, config.bin, issuance.bin. Local/central names, CRC32, lengths, offsets and order must agree; method0, flags0, version-needed20, DOS date0x0021/time0, disks0, exactly one EOCD with five entries. For canonical ZIP metadata, central version-made-by is20 (DOS host0), internal/external attributes0 and start-disk0; local headers start at byte0 and each next local header immediately follows the previous payload. Central directory immediately follows the last payload; EOCD immediately follows the directory. All local/central uncompressed and compressed sizes equal the exact STORE payload length, extras/comments lengths0, central relative offsets exactly locate the corresponding local header, and EOCD directory offset/size describe exactly those five contiguous records. No prefix, holes, overlaps, extraction, path, duplicate, case folding, descriptors, compression, ZIP encryption, ZIP64, links, extras, comments or trailer. These exact canonical metadata choices also require acceptance; they are not inferred historical implementation. CRC is corruption detection, not authentication. Per-entry nonempty caps:16384,16384,8192,4096,4096. Entire plaintext <=65536. Header/directory/name fixed overhead is502 bytes; sum of entry caps49152, so derived inner maximum49654 and outer maximum51042 with maximum SPKI. These are nested byte bounds, not memory credit. STORE requires no decompressor or compression workspace.

config.bin and issuance.bin reuse the exact PROPOSED PACCFG02/PACISS02 version2 TLV grammar: magic8, u16 version, u16 count, then ordered unique u16 tag/u32 length/value, all big endian. No optional/unknown/duplicate/out-of-order tag, gap, padding or trailing bytes. config has exactly16 tags; issuance exactly5. Their tables in docs/integration/complete-manual-client-package-contract-20261018/CONTRACT-PROPOSED.md, SHA256 b77ae570a47e54eb9c1be84ff35b267b447f532fa33c6d2522f259071eb60194, under Restricted ZIP and logical content are incorporated as candidate field definitions, with ONLY the clarifications below. SHA256 fields hash exact complete DER bytes unless explicitly SPKI. Nonzero identities/revisions and strict UTF8/ASCII lengths are mandatory; UTC fields are unsigned seconds, not milliseconds.

Clarification C1: issuance tag1 is exactly the existing issuer view ca_spki_digest, SHA256 of the complete approved CA DER SPKI, NOT a newly invented serialization/hash of an issuer object. Tag2 remains SHA256 of exact CA DER. Together with actual CA/serial/correlation/same-root provenance this identifies the existing approved issuer binding; the digest creates no authority or new identifier. Generation/authority consistency is checked against the existing issuer record before export. This clarification requires explicit review: the older wording approved issuer binding SHA25632 had no defined input domain.

Clarification C2: issuance serial retains the proposed1..20-byte field cap but profile1 accepts only the canonical positive magnitude corresponding to its accepted persisted16-byte prefix+counter; remove redundant leading zeros for this metadata, no sign octet. ASN1 DER INTEGER sign-padding is a separate encoding. Wrong generation/serial/certificate rejects. No counter allocation or replay authority comes from metadata.

Clarification C3: the DNS hostname is exact approved ExpectedServerName, matching the accepted server profile/SAN predicate; no wildcard, IP literal, empty/oversize label, trailing dot or CN fallback. It is candidate data until same-root approval is proved. Server leaf digest is provenance/confirmation, not a mandatory permanent leaf pin or a substitute for actual TLS chain/hostname validation. ALPN is exactly eight ASCII bytes papacc/1. Labels/correlation are1..128 bytes shortest-form valid UTF8 with U0000..001F and U007F..009F excluded, no Unicode normalization. UTC issued_at<=import_not_before<import_expires must fit applicable certificate validity and explicitly approved deployment import policy; certificate90-day cap is not an automatically selected package TTL.

Clarification C4: ca.der is the single profile1 public CA for both channel and direct client issuance, as accepted technical profile1.5 requires. Different channel CA/intermediate chain deployments deny until an accepted extension; do not substitute SYSTEM or origin trust. cliente.der is the exact clientAuth leaf; cliente.pk8 is the matching RSA2048 unencrypted PKCS8v0 only INSIDE the protected plaintext buffer, never a distributed/plaintext temporary file. CA, channel and package private keys never enter it. Initial server/client/signer cert purpose and validity must satisfy their distinct accepted profiles.

## M4 Same-root authority and custody

Use the existing root/issuer/Principal-policy mapping, factual PREPARE/VALIDATE/COMMIT/CURRENT/EPOCH, actual source/issuer pins and serial reservation before private effect. Metadata revision is signed provenance, not remote CURRENT proof. Key generation, issuer signature, protected packaging, export, delivery and Browser import are different factual outcomes. No key-generation side effect on startup or fallback issuer/trust/provider is allowed.

Manual client private key transiently exists only inside the explicitly authorized protected administrative operation. Every password/key/KDF/plaintext/provider copy has an owner, bound, borrower lifetime, wipe and uncertain/retained disposition. No plaintext file, command argument, log, manifest or password recovery record. Protected retained exports require explicit administrative retention duration/capacity and protected same-root staging policy before creation; absence denies retention/export, not unlimited default. No claim of absolute physical erasure, swap/dump exclusion or single-device possession. Wipe only after factual quiescence; no clearing borrowed/retained memory early. Automatic generation/custody remains exclusively local to Browser.

## M5 Import, duplication and retirement

Preserve simple single-package import and advanced separate-file import on the SAME material/candidate/generation/reference/store/gate/ActiveConfiguration/lease pipeline. No second importer authority or persistent database. Authenticate approved signer, perform bounded KDF/AEAD quarantine, validate archive/material/issuer/time/key correspondence and explicit server/trust/recipient confirmation, then use existing transactional draft and commit. Existing material validator alone is not full chain/EKU/time/package validation.

Identical committed package identity/server/full-file hash is an idempotent already-imported result; same package identity with different signed bytes rejects. Renewal/replacement is explicit, with bounded replay/provenance metadata in the same generation and crash-safe commit. No cross-machine offline single-use claim. Cancel before commit preserves old config and wipes only unconsumed owned staging at quiescence. After uncertain commit, reconcile durable selector/result, never pretend rollback or generate a second identity. Retirement requires noncurrent generation, zero leases and factual finalization; Stop/timeout/exit/FINAL do not prove destruction. Persistent server revocation of future authentication remains separate from local removal/delivery. Active Session revocation policy stays pending.

## M6 Administrative CLI, no operational success today

Extend the existing administrative CLI/dispatcher under separate exact functional review; do not create a separate worker or binary/registry merely to implement the examples. Proposed verbs: client package prepare, client package status, client package validate, client package delivered, client revoke. They require actual admin identity, immutable request/client/package correlation, candidate/container/root revision and audit without secrets. No password flags or ENV. delivered records an authorized delivery fact only, not import/remote possession/activation or revoke completion. status distinguishes pending, issued-unpublished, protected, export-uncertain, delivered, revoked and retained according to actual existing records; no string creates those states. validate is bounded offline data/crypto validation, never CURRENT. Actual issuer revocation uses existing transaction, idempotency and separate active-Session policy. Missing CURRENT/CA/crypto/delegation/retention/credit denies effects. These interfaces are PROPOSED, not commands implemented by this record.

